  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">🚫 No computer. We work with the booth.</h2>

  <p>No problem. Most "dead" USBs at the booth are a connection or slot issue, not a dead drive. Fastest checks first:</p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li><strong>Pull the USB out and reseat it firmly.</strong> Wait 10 seconds before re-inserting.</li>
    <li>Try the <strong>other USB slot</strong> on the same player (if it has two).</li>
    <li>Try the <strong>other player</strong>. If it reads there, play from that deck and use Link to share tracks.</li>
    <li>Check the USB tip for <strong>dirt or sweat</strong> — wipe it on your shirt, try again.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Does any player read the USB now?</p>

  <a href="/saved?path=critical&branch=no_laptop" class="btn btn-go" data-event="outcome_reached" data-outcome="saved" data-path="critical">
    🟢 Yes — it's reading
  </a>
  <a href="/protocol/critical/no-laptop-2" class="btn btn-stop" data-event="step_completed" data-step="no_laptop_1" data-answer="no">
    🔴 No — still nothing
  </a>
</Tunnel>
